module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ConstantSheafModules
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LeftExact
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.StdBasis

/-!
# Homomorphisms out of a finitely presented module and sections of constant sheaves

Let `(C, J)` be a site and `R` a commutative ring. For an object `U` of the site, taking the
sections over `U` of the constant sheaf generated by an `R`-module is the functor
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSections J U`, which is exact. This file uses that exactness to
compute the sections of the constant sheaf on a module of homomorphisms: for a finitely presented
`R`-module `M` and any `R`-module `N`,
`Γ(U, Hom_R(M, N)̲) = Hom_R(M, Γ(U, N̲))`.

This is the computation that Stacks Tag 093T (1) reduces to object by object: there the assertion
is the isomorphism of sheaves `Hom_R(M, N)̲ = SheafHom(M̲, N̲)`, and its proof is exactly the
reduction performed here — present `M` by a finite free resolution, turn the presentation into a
left exact sequence by applying `Hom_R(-, N)`, and use that taking sections of a constant sheaf is
exact and commutes with finite powers.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.presentationHomPi`: for a presentation `R^m → R^n → M → 0`, the map
  `(M →ₗ[R] X) →ₗ[R] (Fin n → X)` reading a homomorphism on the chosen generators of `M`.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.presentationRelPi`: the induced map `(Fin n → X) →ₗ[R] (Fin m → X)`, whose
  kernel is the image of `presentationHomPi`.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.evalHom`: evaluation of homomorphisms, as a linear map in the argument.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSectionsPiEquiv`: the splitting
  `Γ(U, (Fin n → N)̲) ≃ₗ[R] (Fin n → Γ(U, N̲))`.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.homComparison`: the canonical comparison
  `Γ(U, E̲) →ₗ[R] (M →ₗ[R] Γ(U, N̲))` attached to a linear equivalence `(M →ₗ[R] N) ≃ₗ[R] E`,
  specified on a section `s` and an element `m` by applying `Γ(U, -̲)` to evaluation at `m`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.small_linearMap_of_finite`: a module of homomorphisms out of a finite
  module has a representative in the universe of the target.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.range_presentationHomPi`: `Hom_R(M, X)` is the kernel of the relation map
  of any finite presentation of `M`, naturally in `X`. This is left exactness of `Hom_R(-, X)`,
  read off on generators.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.range_constantSections_map_eq_ker_of_injective`: `constantSections` takes
  an exact pair whose first map is *injective* to an exact pair, using only `HasSheafify` for
  modules.
* `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.bijective_homComparison`: the comparison
  `Γ(U, Hom_R(M, N)̲) → Hom_R(M, Γ(U, N̲))` is bijective when `M` is finitely presented.

## Implementation notes

**No `@[stacks]` attribute appears in this file, deliberately.** The tagged statement of Tag 093T
is an isomorphism of *sheaves* `Hom_R(M, N)̲ ≅ SheafHom(M̲, N̲)`, and that is not proved here:
assembling the objectwise computation below into a sheaf isomorphism additionally needs the
internal hom of sheaves of modules over the slice sites together with the identification
`SheafHom(M̲, N̲)(U) = Hom(M̲|_U, N̲|_U)` and the compatibility of the constant sheaf with
restriction to a slice site. Tagging this file would be a false coverage claim.

The hypotheses are weaker than those of the companion Tag 093K in
`ConstantSheafModules.lean`. Only `HasSheafify J (ModuleCat.{x} R)` is used, i.e. weak
sheafification together with its left exactness, and the `Type`-level sheafification trio that
Tag 093K needs is *not* required. The reason is structural: the half of exactness that needs a
set-theoretic section of a surjection — hence the constant sheaf of sets — is surjectivity on
sections, and the present argument never uses it. The module of homomorphisms is a *kernel*, so
`range_constantSections_kerSubtype` suffices, and the comparison between an abstract injection with
the right image and the canonical kernel inclusion is an isomorphism of modules rather than merely
a surjection. That is what `range_constantSections_map_eq_ker_of_injective` records.

`presentationHomPi` and `presentationRelPi` are stated for an arbitrary module `X`, not only for
`N`, because the argument instantiates them twice: at `N`, to present the module whose constant
sheaf is taken, and at `Γ(U, N̲)`, to present the module of homomorphisms into the sections. Both
instantiations are the same two linear maps, which is what makes the comparison square commute.

Universes: the site (`u`, `v`), the ring (`w`), the sections (`x`) and the finitely presented
module (`y`) stay independent; nothing in the statements forces `x` to contain `max u v`.
`small_linearMap_of_finite` is what makes an instantiation with `E` in universe `x` possible,
exactly as `small_tensorProduct_of_finite` does for Tag 093K.

What discharging the one hypothesis costs, recorded because it is easy to overstate:
`HasSheafify J (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R)` *is* available for a completely general site and
commutative ring, but it does **not** follow from `infer_instance` alone. Mathlib's generic
instance additionally needs `PreservesColimitsOfShape (J.Cover X)ᵒᵖ` for
`forget (ModuleCat.{max u v w} R)`,
whose only route is the size shrink `preservesFilteredColimitsOfSize_of_univLE`, and that is a
lemma rather than an instance. Supplying it once makes `HasSheafify` synthesize, so the hypothesis
is genuinely free at `x = max u v w` — just not automatic.

The comparison is packaged as a subtype carrying its characterizing equation, matching
`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.tensorComparison`, so that a consumer gets both the map and the formula for
its values without unfolding the construction.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 093J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093J)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 093K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 093T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093T)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite

universe u v w x y

namespace Stacks.ConstantSheaf

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
variable {R : Type w} [CommRing R]

/-! ### Left exactness of `Hom_R(-, X)` along a finite presentation -/

section Presentation

variable {n m : ℕ} {M : Type y} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]

/-- Reading a homomorphism out of `M` on the generators `ψ (Pi.single i 1)` supplied by a finite
presentation `ψ : R^n → M`. -/
noncomputable def presentationHomPi (ψ : (Fin n → R) →ₗ[R] M)
    (X : Type*) [AddCommGroup X] [Module R X] :
    (M →ₗ[R] X) →ₗ[R] (Fin n → X) :=
  (Module.piEquiv (Fin n) R X).symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ LinearMap.lcomp R X ψ

/-- The `i`-th coordinate of `presentationHomPi ψ X g` is the value of `g` on the generator
`ψ (Pi.single i 1)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem presentationHomPi_apply (ψ : (Fin n → R) →ₗ[R] M)
    (X : Type*) [AddCommGroup X] [Module R X] (g : M →ₗ[R] X) (i : Fin n) :
    presentationHomPi ψ X g i = g (ψ (Pi.single i 1)) := by
  simp [presentationHomPi, Module.piEquiv]

/-- The relation map of a finite presentation, read on the chosen generators: the matrix of
`a : R^m → R^n` acting on an `n`-tuple of elements of `X`. -/
noncomputable def presentationRelPi (a : (Fin m → R) →ₗ[R] (Fin n → R))
    (X : Type*) [AddCommGroup X] [Module R X] :
    (Fin n → X) →ₗ[R] (Fin m → X) :=
  (Module.piEquiv (Fin m) R X).symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ LinearMap.lcomp R X a ∘ₗ
    (Module.piEquiv (Fin n) R X).toLinearMap

/-- The `j`-th coordinate of `presentationRelPi a X v` is `∑ i, a (Pi.single j 1) i • v i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem presentationRelPi_apply (a : (Fin m → R) →ₗ[R] (Fin n → R))
    (X : Type*) [AddCommGroup X] [Module R X] (v : Fin n → X) (j : Fin m) :
    presentationRelPi a X v j = ∑ i, a (Pi.single j 1) i • v i := by
  simp [presentationRelPi, Module.piEquiv]

/-- Homomorphisms out of `M` are determined by their values on the generators. -/
theorem presentationHomPi_injective {ψ : (Fin n → R) →ₗ[R] M} (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ)
    (X : Type*) [AddCommGroup X] [Module R X] :
    Function.Injective (presentationHomPi ψ X) := by
  intro g g' h
  refine LinearMap.lcomp_injective_of_surjective (S := R) (N := X) ψ hψ ?_
  exact (Module.piEquiv (Fin n) R X).symm.injective h

/-- **Left exactness of `Hom_R(-, X)`**, read off on the generators of a finite presentation
`R^m → R^n → M → 0`: the image of `Hom_R(M, X)` in `X^n` is exactly the kernel of the relation
map. -/
theorem range_presentationHomPi {ψ : (Fin n → R) →ₗ[R] M} {a : (Fin m → R) →ₗ[R] (Fin n → R)}
    (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ) (hexact : Function.Exact a ψ)
    (X : Type*) [AddCommGroup X] [Module R X] :
    LinearMap.range (presentationHomPi ψ X) = LinearMap.ker (presentationRelPi a X) := by
  have hk : LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.lcomp R X a) = LinearMap.range (LinearMap.lcomp R X ψ) :=
    LinearMap.exact_iff.mp (LinearMap.exact_lcomp_of_exact_of_surjective X hexact hψ)
  ext v
  have h1 : presentationRelPi a X v = 0 ↔
      LinearMap.lcomp R X a (Module.piEquiv (Fin n) R X v) = 0 := by
    simp only [presentationRelPi, LinearMap.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe]
    exact (Module.piEquiv (Fin m) R X).symm.map_eq_zero_iff
  have h2 : (∃ g, presentationHomPi ψ X g = v) ↔
      ∃ g, LinearMap.lcomp R X ψ g = Module.piEquiv (Fin n) R X v := by
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨g, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨g, by simp [presentationHomPi]⟩
    · rintro ⟨g, hg⟩
      exact ⟨g, by simp [presentationHomPi, hg]⟩
  rw [LinearMap.mem_range, LinearMap.mem_ker, h1, h2, ← LinearMap.mem_range, ← LinearMap.mem_ker,
    hk]

end Presentation

/-! ### Modules of homomorphisms out of a finite module stay small -/

/-- A module of homomorphisms out of a finitely generated module does not enlarge the universe
needed to represent the target: `Hom_R(M, N)` embeds into a finite power of `N`. -/
theorem small_linearMap_of_finite (M : ModuleCat.{y} R) (N : ModuleCat.{x} R)
    [Module.Finite R M] : Small.{x} ((M : Type y) →ₗ[R] (N : Type x)) := by
  obtain ⟨n, f, hf⟩ := Module.Finite.exists_fin' R (M : Type y)
  exact small_of_injective (presentationHomPi_injective hf (N : Type x))

/-! ### Sections of a constant sheaf on a finite power -/

section PiEquiv

variable [HasWeakSheafify J (ModuleCat.{x} R)]

/-- The sections over `U` of the constant sheaf on a finite power of `N` are the corresponding
finite power of the sections of the constant sheaf on `N`. -/
noncomputable def constantSectionsPiEquiv (U : C) (n : ℕ) (N : ModuleCat.{x} R) :
    ((constantSections J U).obj (ModuleCat.of R (Fin n → N)) : Type x) ≃ₗ[R]
      (Fin n → ((constantSections J U).obj N : Type x)) :=
  LinearEquiv.ofLinearMap
    (LinearMap.pi fun i => ((constantSections J U).map (piProj N i)).hom)
    (∑ i : Fin n, ((constantSections J U).map (piIncl N i)).hom ∘ₗ LinearMap.proj i)
    (LinearMap.ext fun w => funext fun j => by
      simpa using constantSections_piProj_sum J U N w j)
    (LinearMap.ext fun z => by
      simpa using (constantSections_eq_sum_piIncl J U N z).symm)

/-- The `i`-th coordinate of `constantSectionsPiEquiv J U n N z` is the image of `z` under the
sections of the projection `piProj N i`. -/
@[simp]
theorem constantSectionsPiEquiv_apply (U : C) (n : ℕ) (N : ModuleCat.{x} R)
    (z : (constantSections J U).obj (ModuleCat.of R (Fin n → N))) (i : Fin n) :
    constantSectionsPiEquiv J U n N z i = ((constantSections J U).map (piProj N i)).hom z :=
  rfl

/-- A morphism between finite powers of `N` with matrix entries `A` acts on sections of the
constant sheaves by the same matrix. -/
theorem constantSectionsPiEquiv_map (U : C) {n m : ℕ} (N : ModuleCat.{x} R)
    (cc : ModuleCat.of R (Fin n → N) ⟶ ModuleCat.of R (Fin m → N)) (A : Fin n → Fin m → R)
    (hcc : ∀ i j, piIncl N i ≫ cc ≫ piProj N j = A i j • 𝟙 N)
    (z : (constantSections J U).obj (ModuleCat.of R (Fin n → N))) (j : Fin m) :
    constantSectionsPiEquiv J U m N (((constantSections J U).map cc).hom z) j =
      ∑ i, A i j • constantSectionsPiEquiv J U n N z i := by
  have key := constantSections_piProj_comp J U N cc A hcc
    (fun i => ((constantSections J U).map (piProj N i)).hom z) j
  rwa [← constantSections_eq_sum_piIncl J U N z] at key

end PiEquiv

/-! ### An exact pair with injective first map -/

section Exact

variable [HasSheafify J (ModuleCat.{x} R)]

/-- `constantSections` takes an exact pair whose first map is injective to an exact pair.

This is a sharpening of `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.range_constantSections_map_eq_ker` in the
hypotheses rather than in the conclusion: injectivity makes the comparison with the canonical
kernel inclusion an isomorphism, so no surjectivity statement about sections — and hence none of
the `Type`-level sheafification hypotheses — is needed. -/
theorem range_constantSections_map_eq_ker_of_injective (U : C) {A B D : ModuleCat.{x} R}
    (α : A ⟶ B) (β : B ⟶ D) (hα : Function.Injective α.hom)
    (h : LinearMap.range α.hom = LinearMap.ker β.hom) :
    LinearMap.range ((constantSections J U).map α).hom =
      LinearMap.ker ((constantSections J U).map β).hom := by
  have hmem (a : A) : α.hom a ∈ LinearMap.ker β.hom := h ▸ LinearMap.mem_range_self _ a
  have hbij : Function.Bijective (LinearMap.codRestrict (LinearMap.ker β.hom) α.hom hmem) := by
    refine ⟨fun a a' hh => hα (congrArg Subtype.val hh), fun z => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ : (z : B) ∈ LinearMap.range α.hom := by rw [h]; exact z.2
    exact ⟨a, Subtype.ext ha⟩
  let eiso : A ≅ ModuleCat.of R (LinearMap.ker β.hom) :=
    (LinearEquiv.ofBijective _ hbij).toModuleIso
  have hfac : eiso.hom ≫ ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.ker β.hom).subtype = α := by
    ext a
    rfl
  rw [← hfac, (constantSections J U (R := R)).map_comp, ModuleCat.hom_comp,
    LinearMap.range_comp_of_range_eq_top _
      (LinearMap.range_eq_top.mpr ((ModuleCat.epi_iff_surjective _).mp inferInstance))]
  exact range_constantSections_kerSubtype J U β

end Exact

/-! ### Sections of the constant sheaf on a module of homomorphisms -/

section Hom

/-- Evaluation of homomorphisms, as a linear map in the argument: `m ↦ (f ↦ f m)`. -/
noncomputable def evalHom (M : Type y) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (N : Type x) [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] :
    M →ₗ[R] ((M →ₗ[R] N) →ₗ[R] N) :=
  (LinearMap.id : (M →ₗ[R] N) →ₗ[R] M →ₗ[R] N).flip

/-- `evalHom M N mm` sends a homomorphism `f : M →ₗ[R] N` to `f mm`. -/
@[simp]
theorem evalHom_apply (M : Type y) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (N : Type x) [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] (mm : M) (f : M →ₗ[R] N) :
    evalHom M N mm f = f mm :=
  rfl

variable [HasWeakSheafify J (ModuleCat.{x} R)]

/-- The canonical comparison for a module `E` representing `Hom_R(M, N)` in the universe where
sections are taken. Its value at a section `s` and an element `m` of `M` is obtained by applying
the sections functor to evaluation at `m`. -/
noncomputable def homComparison (M : ModuleCat.{y} R) (N E : ModuleCat.{x} R)
    (e : ((M : Type y) →ₗ[R] (N : Type x)) ≃ₗ[R] E) (U : C) :
    { f : ((constantSections J U).obj E) →ₗ[R]
        ((M : Type y) →ₗ[R] ((constantSections J U).obj N)) //
      ∀ (s : (constantSections J U).obj E) (mm : M),
        f s mm = ((constantSections J U).map (ModuleCat.ofHom
          (LinearMap.lcomp R (N : Type x) e.symm.toLinearMap
            (evalHom (M : Type y) (N : Type x) mm)))).hom s } :=
  ⟨(constantSectionsMapLinear J E N U ∘ₗ LinearMap.lcomp R (N : Type x) e.symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ
    evalHom (M : Type y) (N : Type x)).flip, fun _ _ => rfl⟩

end Hom

section Bijective

variable [HasSheafify J (ModuleCat.{x} R)]

/-- **The sections core of Stacks Tag 093T (1).** For a finitely presented module `M` and any
module `N`, taking sections over `U` of the constant sheaf on `Hom_R(M, N)` gives
`Hom_R(M, Γ(U, N̲))`: the canonical comparison is bijective.

This is not tagged `@[stacks 093T]`; see the implementation notes of this file. -/
theorem bijective_homComparison (M : ModuleCat.{y} R) [Module.FinitePresentation R (M : Type y)]
    (N E : ModuleCat.{x} R) (e : ((M : Type y) →ₗ[R] (N : Type x)) ≃ₗ[R] E) (U : C) :
    Function.Bijective (homComparison J M N E e U).1 := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨n, k, ψ, a, hψ, hexact⟩ := Module.FinitePresentation.exists_fin' R (M : Type y)
  -- the presentation of `Hom_R(M, N)` as a kernel, transported to the chosen representative `E`
  let α : E ⟶ ModuleCat.of R (Fin n → N) :=
    ModuleCat.ofHom (presentationHomPi ψ (N : Type x) ∘ₗ e.symm.toLinearMap)
  let β : ModuleCat.of R (Fin n → N) ⟶ ModuleCat.of R (Fin k → N) :=
    ModuleCat.ofHom (presentationRelPi a (N : Type x))
  have hαinj : Function.Injective α.hom :=
    (presentationHomPi_injective hψ (N : Type x)).comp e.symm.injective
  have hrange : LinearMap.range α.hom = LinearMap.ker β.hom := by
    show LinearMap.range (presentationHomPi ψ (N : Type x) ∘ₗ e.symm.toLinearMap) = _
    rw [LinearMap.range_comp_of_range_eq_top _ e.symm.range]
    exact range_presentationHomPi hψ hexact (N : Type x)
  have hker := range_constantSections_map_eq_ker_of_injective J U α β hαinj hrange
  -- the matrix of `β`, which is the matrix of the relation map on any module
  have hcc : ∀ (i : Fin n) (j : Fin k),
      piIncl N i ≫ β ≫ piProj N j = a (Pi.single j 1) i • 𝟙 N := by
    intro i j
    apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
    apply LinearMap.ext
    intro b
    show presentationRelPi a (N : Type x) (Pi.single i b) j = _
    rw [presentationRelPi_apply]
    simp [Pi.single_apply, Finset.sum_ite_eq']
  -- the splitting of the sections of the constant sheaves on the finite powers
  have hconj : ∀ z, constantSectionsPiEquiv J U k N (((constantSections J U).map β).hom z) =
      presentationRelPi a ((constantSections J U).obj N : Type x)
        (constantSectionsPiEquiv J U n N z) := by
    intro z
    funext j
    rw [constantSectionsPiEquiv_map J U N β (fun i j => a (Pi.single j 1) i) hcc z j,
      presentationRelPi_apply]
  -- the comparison square: reading the comparison on the generators of `M` is `Γ(U, α̲)`
  have hsq : ∀ s, presentationHomPi ψ ((constantSections J U).obj N : Type x)
      ((homComparison J M N E e U).1 s) =
        constantSectionsPiEquiv J U n N (((constantSections J U).map α).hom s) := by
    intro s
    funext i
    have hmor : ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.lcomp R (N : Type x) e.symm.toLinearMap
        (evalHom (M : Type y) (N : Type x) (ψ (Pi.single i 1)))) = α ≫ piProj N i := by
      ext t
      show (e.symm t) (ψ (Pi.single i 1)) = presentationHomPi ψ (N : Type x) (e.symm t) i
      rw [presentationHomPi_apply]
    rw [presentationHomPi_apply, constantSectionsPiEquiv_apply,
      (homComparison J M N E e U).2 s (ψ (Pi.single i 1)), hmor,
      CategoryTheory.Functor.map_comp, ModuleCat.comp_apply]
  refine ⟨fun s s' hss => ?_, fun g => ?_⟩
  · exact injective_constantSections_map J α hαinj U
      ((constantSectionsPiEquiv J U n N).injective (by rw [← hsq, ← hsq, hss]))
  · have hg : presentationHomPi ψ ((constantSections J U).obj N : Type x) g ∈
        LinearMap.ker (presentationRelPi a ((constantSections J U).obj N : Type x)) := by
      rw [← range_presentationHomPi hψ hexact]
      exact LinearMap.mem_range_self _ g
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ : (constantSectionsPiEquiv J U n N).symm
        (presentationHomPi ψ ((constantSections J U).obj N : Type x) g) ∈
          LinearMap.range ((constantSections J U).map α).hom := by
      rw [hker, LinearMap.mem_ker]
      refine (constantSectionsPiEquiv J U k N).injective ?_
      rw [hconj, LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply, map_zero]
      exact hg
    refine ⟨s, presentationHomPi_injective hψ _ ?_⟩
    rw [hsq s, hs, LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply]

end Bijective

end Stacks.ConstantSheaf
